From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 04:04:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: samsung: Add Exynos9820 power domain support

The Exynos9820 power domain block is the familiar one - a CONFIGURATION
register with the power request and a STATUS register 4 bytes above it -
but only bit 0 is defined, unlike the 0x7/0xf masks of Exynos4210 and
Exynos5433.

The mask comes from the vendor PMU tables: LineageOS/
android_kernel_samsung_exynos9820, commit 7d08ec364a06, drivers/soc/
samsung/cal-if/exynos9820/flexpmu_cal_local_exynos9820.h, dpu_on[] and
dpu_off[] write bit 0 of DPU_CONFIGURATION and poll bit 0 of DPU_STATUS.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/samsung/exynos-pm-domains.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/samsung/exynos-pm-domains.c b/drivers/pmdomain/samsung/exynos-pm-domains.c
index 5c3aa898308..5d6da607da4 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/samsung/exynos-pm-domains.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/samsung/exynos-pm-domains.c
@@ -81,6 +81,10 @@ static const struct exynos_pm_domain_config exynos5433_cfg = {
 	.local_pwr_cfg		= 0xf,
 };
 
+static const struct exynos_pm_domain_config exynos9820_cfg = {
+	.local_pwr_cfg		= 0x1,
+};
+
 static const struct of_device_id exynos_pm_domain_of_match[] = {
 	{
 		.compatible = "samsung,exynos4210-pd",
@@ -88,6 +92,9 @@ static const struct of_device_id exynos_pm_domain_of_match[] = {
 	}, {
 		.compatible = "samsung,exynos5433-pd",
 		.data = &exynos5433_cfg,
+	}, {
+		.compatible = "samsung,exynos9820-pd",
+		.data = &exynos9820_cfg,
 	},
 	{ },
 };
